  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="work" n="88">
        <pb n="128"/>
        <head>88 — i — I. — <quote>The Lord hath done great things for us and we have been in joy</quote><ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a1" target="#n1" n="1"/>.</head>
        <div type="preface">
          <ab n="1">Again Other Hymns Sung on the Same Night Preceding Sunday after the Reading of the Gospel.</ab>
        </div>
        <div type="section">
          <ab n="2">Our ears have been filled with joy; we have received a divine change; [and our minds have been enlightened<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a2" target="#n2" n="2"/> by the splendour that flashes <pb n="129"/> from the angels<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a3" target="#n3" n="3"/> that sit by the tomb. From the grave itself we have drawn incorruptibility; from the closed gates of <placeName>Sheol</placeName> resurrection and life. Who is he that will not mortify<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a4" target="#n4" n="4"/> his<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a5" target="#n5" n="5"/> limbs that are upon the earth? who is there that will not praise him that in all things is God, him that is exalted<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a6" target="#n6" n="6"/>, him that is earthly<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a7" target="#n7" n="7"/> in the flesh, and again re-ascended and took his place [in the heights? Whom let us all beg<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a8" target="#n8" n="8"/> and entreat to be with us in his mercy until<ptr type="noteAnchor" xml:id="a9" target="#n9" n="9"/> the end of the world.</ab>
        </div>
      </div>
      <noteGrp>
        <note xml:id="n1" target="#a1" n="1"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 128, n. 4</orig></choice> Ps. cxxv, 3.</note>
        <note xml:id="n2" target="#a2" n="2"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 128, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>we have been illuminated</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n3" target="#a3" n="3"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 1</orig></choice> John xx, 11, 12 (verbal diff.).</note>
        <note xml:id="n4" target="#a4" n="4"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 2</orig></choice> Col. iii, 5, 6 <quote>Mortify therefore..... fornication and filthiness of passions..... disobedience.</quote></note>
        <note xml:id="n5" target="#a5" n="5"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 3</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>the</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n6" target="#a6" n="6"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 4</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>above</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n7" target="#a7" n="7"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 5</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>below</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n8" target="#a8" n="8"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 6</orig></choice> Corr. <quote>ask</quote>.</note>
        <note xml:id="n9" target="#a9" n="9"><choice><reg/><orig>p. 129, n. 7</orig></choice> Matth. xxviii, 20 <quote>And lo! I am with you until the end of the world.</quote></note>
      </noteGrp>
